WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.503
Here is the key insight.

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:07.086
In the real world,

00:00:07.166 --> 00:00:10.669
an attacker cannot conjure a different graph for
every node they want to fool.

00:00:10.749 --> 00:00:14.252
They inject one perturbed graph,

00:00:14.332 --> 00:00:17.835
and that single graph has to disrupt the entire set
of target nodes at the same time.

00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:21.418
If we certify the whole target set jointly instead
of one node at a time,

00:00:21.498 --> 00:00:25.001
the guarantee should be much stronger.

00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:28.584
Prior collective methods existed for
edge-modification attacks,

00:00:28.664 --> 00:00:32.167
but they assume a fixed receptive field and simply
do not carry over to injection attacks,

00:00:32.247 --> 00:00:35.750
which expand the receptive field by adding new edges.
